  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for patchy frost Saturday night across\nthe north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will be building in Saturday evening from Canada.\nMovement of the high will determine how low temps can drop\nSaturday night into Sunday morning. Confidence in frost\npotential has decreased due to ensemble models pointing to a\nthicker cloud deck much earlier in the evening. Upper air model\nsoundings indicate the weak winds at the surface, however,\nsurface dewpoints should be much lower. Thus, lower RH values\nwhich should keep frost potential low. Due to the uncertainty,\nkept frost in the forecast for consistency.",
